{
  "comment": "Build matrix for build.yml. 'include' is the CMake 'mujoco' job matrix and 'bazel' is the 'bazel' job matrix. 'tier' controls when an entry runs: 'core' runs on every pull_request and push; 'extended' runs only on push to main (full compiler sweep, and the oldest supported and latest Bazel versions). 'ccache' controls compiler caching in 'mujoco' jobs. 'extended' postsubmit-only jobs disable 'ccache' and 'disk_cache' to reduce per-push churn against GitHub's 10 GiB cache limit. For Bazel, an empty 'bazel_version' means the version pinned in .bazelversion, and 'disk_cache' keeps a Bazel disk cache across runs (see build.yml). See generate_matrix() in build_steps.sh.",
